  "complexity": 5,
  "title": "S2a v2: route a provider=\"claude\" row (id claude:<tier>) through the existing Claude fallback path with the row's tier",
  "spec": "Goal T-1334 (S1 T-1352 merged). Replaces T-1356 after spec review T-1358 (reservation keyed on the row id, tier=row id leaking into t[\"tier\"] readers, missing review_rule, unreleased reservation on early returns). New design: a Claude executor row's id is \"claude:<tier>\" with <tier> an alias in [models] (e.g. id \"claude:opus\"). That id is exactly the executor value the existing fallback path already writes (spawn.py:1564 f\"claude:{tier}\"), so dispatch reuses executor._exhausted()'s tested machinery (account pick, reservation handoff to run_worker, review_rule, running_claude_workers counting) with the row's tier instead of fallback_tier(complexity). t[\"tier\"] stays a real [models] alias; spawn.run_worker is unchanged.\n\n1. orchestrator/pool.py Pool._read_executors (uses executor_rows from S1): a provider=\"claude\" row is valid only if its id is \"claude:<tier>\", tier in (\"haiku\",\"sonnet\",\"opus\"), cfg[\"models\"][tier] is a str, and its model is absent or equal to cfg[\"models\"][tier] (absent -> set to that value). An invalid claude row is loaded with enabled=False and hold_reason \"invalid claude row: <reason>\", plus one stderr line; never raise at load.\n2. orchestrator/executor.py _exhausted(pool, t, run=None, tier=None): tier None keeps today's behaviour exactly (policy + fallback_tier). tier given (routed claude row): skip the on_exhausted policy check, use that tier, same pool.pick(\"execute\") (None -> held, hold_reason \"no account with headroom\"), same bus.update(tier=tier, fallback=\"claude\", review_rule=...), same thread + reservation handoff.\n3. executor.start (executor.py:487): if ex is not None and ex.provider == \"claude\": ex.roll_day(); ex.day_tasks += 1; pool.save(); result = _exhausted(pool, t, tier=ex.id.split(\":\", 1)[1]); handed_off = result.get(\"status\") == \"fallback\"; return result. elif ex is None or ex.provider == \"codex\"-unavailable: unchanged. Any other provider -> held, hold_reason \"unknown executor provider <p>\" (release as the finally already does).\n4. No change to spawn.py, run_worker, reservation code, review routing or t[\"tier\"] readers: all already handle \"claude:<tier>\".\nTests (unittest.TestCase methods): start with only a claude:opus row eligible calls the worker with an account_id, sets tier \"opus\" and fallback \"claude\", and pool.executors[\"claude:opus\"].day_tasks increments; routed dispatch ignores on_exhausted=\"hold\"; no account headroom -> held; invalid claude rows (bad id, unknown tier, model mismatch) load disabled with the reason; a valid row without model gets cfg models[tier]; existing tests/test_executor.py _exhausted cases unchanged. No pool.toml edit, no new dependencies. Additive; git revert restores Codex-only routing.",
  "inputs": [],
